# Environment variables and sensitive data — never commit these.
#
# The globs are deliberately broad rather than an enumerated list, so variants
# nobody thought of are covered too: .env.production.local, .env.bak, .env.old,
# env_backup.env. Neither glob is anchored to the repository root, so they apply
# at any depth — ethics-dash/.env.local is caught by the same rules.
.env
.env.*
*.env
.envrc

# ...with one exception: the template holds placeholders, not real values, and
# is meant to be committed. This negation has to stay below the globs above,
# because the last matching pattern is the one that wins.
!.env.example

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
.virtualenv/

# Python cache and compiled files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.Python

# IDE and editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs and databases
*.log
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

